WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.393
Welcome to ADVISIO.

2
00:00:01.823 --> 00:00:05.039
Explore the Researcher workspace and
its core features throughout

3
00:00:05.074 --> 00:00:06.084
this walkthrough.

4
00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:09.767
The Overview displays information
about your research project.

5
00:00:10.266 --> 00:00:13.645
This demonstration follows CampusWay
and Research Group A.

6
00:00:14.144 --> 00:00:17.011
The project panel identifies the
current research stage.

7
00:00:17.441 --> 00:00:21.087
Other sections display milestone
progress, requirements, upcoming

8
00:00:21.122 --> 00:00:24.465
consultation information, and recent
updates when those records are

9
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.568
available.

10
00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:29.731
The sidebar connects the research
workspace, academic activities,

11
00:00:29.824 --> 00:00:31.183
and communication areas.

12
00:00:31.775 --> 00:00:35.943
My Project, Tasks, Documents, Group
Files, and Timeline

13
00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:37.765
refer to the research workflow.

14
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.491
Defense, My Grades, Consultations, and
Calendar show related

15
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.582
academic records.

16
00:00:44.012 --> 00:00:45.718
The example has one project.

17
00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.004
A project selector appears where
multiple authorized projects

18
00:00:49.062 --> 00:00:50.409
require a selection.

19
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.982
Open My Project to inspect the title,
project details, assigned

20
00:00:55.005 --> 00:00:57.130
adviser, and current workflow.

21
00:00:57.815 --> 00:01:00.694
A project contains the research work
and participants.

22
00:01:01.286 --> 00:01:04.746
Its configured workflow defines the
stages and requirements used to

23
00:01:04.804 --> 00:01:05.756
track that work.

24
00:01:06.348 --> 00:01:09.367
This demonstration project is already
enrolled in its assigned

25
00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:10.226
workflow.

26
00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:13.886
Select My Group to inspect membership
and the group leader.

27
00:01:14.316 --> 00:01:17.578
This example uses a fictional research
team and adviser.

28
00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:21.526
Team and adviser-request actions
depend on leadership and assignment

29
00:01:21.561 --> 00:01:22.118
status.

30
00:01:22.547 --> 00:01:25.137
This project already has an accepted
adviser.

31
00:01:25.566 --> 00:01:28.538
The group area connects these
participants to the same research

32
00:01:28.585 --> 00:01:29.363
project.

33
00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:33.589
Tasks lists the requirements
associated with the enrolled workflow.

34
00:01:34.019 --> 00:01:37.421
Inspect each item's status, deadline,
and milestone.

35
00:01:38.013 --> 00:01:41.380
In this prepared workspace, the
initial scope requirement has been

36
00:01:41.403 --> 00:01:44.445
approved and the research proposal
requires revision.

37
00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:48.172
Later requirements may be locked until
the configured prerequisites

38
00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:49.089
are satisfied.

39
00:01:49.681 --> 00:01:52.897
A completed item and a future item
therefore represent different

40
00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:54.627
points in the same workflow.

41
00:01:55.233 --> 00:01:57.125
Open Revised research proposal.

42
00:01:57.555 --> 00:02:00.504
Read its instructions before selecting
a file or document.

43
00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:04.324
The detail workspace connects the
requirement to its submission,

44
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.168
faculty feedback, and milestone
information.

45
00:02:07.853 --> 00:02:10.790
Review the recorded guidance about
route-selection rules and the

46
00:02:10.837 --> 00:02:12.532
requirements-to-test matrix.

47
00:02:13.031 --> 00:02:15.202
Faculty resources appear when
attached;

48
00:02:15.515 --> 00:02:16.804
none are prepared here.

49
00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.554
The next chapter follows this task
into the document and revision

50
00:02:20.612 --> 00:02:21.471
submission.

51
00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:25.213
Documents contains working files and
records associated with

52
00:02:25.283 --> 00:02:26.398
research requirements.

53
00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:30.972
Open Research proposal to inspect its
lifecycle status, milestone,

54
00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.330
and available versions.

55
00:02:32.922 --> 00:02:36.138
A working document and a submitted
version have different purposes:

56
00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:39.516
the working file can be prepared for a
requirement, while the

57
00:02:39.563 --> 00:02:43.197
submitted record identifies the
version sent for faculty review.

58
00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.585
Select version one to inspect the
earlier submitted snapshot, then

59
00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.129
open its Feedback tab.

60
00:02:49.814 --> 00:02:52.751
This prepared version shows no
feedback in the current document

61
00:02:52.786 --> 00:02:53.274
viewer.

62
00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:57.151
Return to version two to inspect its
active review assignment.

63
00:02:57.744 --> 00:03:00.553
The task page contains the prepared
revision guidance.

64
00:03:01.145 --> 00:03:03.816
Feedback belongs to the version on
which it is recorded;

65
00:03:04.315 --> 00:03:07.264
selecting a later version does not
move earlier comments to that

66
00:03:07.322 --> 00:03:07.856
version.

67
00:03:08.448 --> 00:03:11.501
Where linked review comments are
available, the feedback area

68
00:03:11.559 --> 00:03:13.661
displays them with their recorded
state.

69
00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:17.657
The Add menu includes working-file
upload and Google document

70
00:03:17.704 --> 00:03:18.307
options.

71
00:03:18.899 --> 00:03:22.487
A working-file upload can be
associated with a milestone, but

72
00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:25.006
uploading alone does not submit it for
review.

73
00:03:25.691 --> 00:03:28.989
Google document creation and connected
operations require an

74
00:03:29.024 --> 00:03:30.231
available integration.

75
00:03:30.661 --> 00:03:33.041
This demonstration uses a local PDF;

76
00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.444
no Google connection is established.

77
00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:39.841
Return to the proposal task and select
the prepared revision PDF.

78
00:03:40.433 --> 00:03:43.556
Review the file, requirement, and
project in the submission

79
00:03:43.614 --> 00:03:45.356
confirmation before confirming.

80
00:03:45.948 --> 00:03:49.048
The application records the revision
for the group and displays the

81
00:03:49.106 --> 00:03:50.488
resulting submission state.

82
00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.787
Submission does not mean approval.

83
00:03:53.216 --> 00:03:56.432
Faculty review determines the later
decision, and the workflow

84
00:03:56.479 --> 00:03:58.243
applies its configured requirements.

85
00:03:58.743 --> 00:04:02.493
This connects the task, document
version, submission, and review

86
00:04:02.562 --> 00:04:03.479
process.

87
00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.586
Official documents are a separate
published record.

88
00:04:07.178 --> 00:04:10.325
This prepared Researcher workspace has
no official copies.

89
00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.645
Researchers can inspect copies made
available to them;

90
00:04:14.144 --> 00:04:18.022
approval, signing, and finalization
are not demonstrated through

91
00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:18.731
this role.

92
00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:22.655
Use the task's submission history and
document versions to inspect

93
00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:25.708
what was sent and any feedback that
becomes available.

94
00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.156
Group Files stores shared working
material in folders.

95
00:04:29.586 --> 00:04:33.440
Create a folder, open it, and add the
demonstration PDF.

96
00:04:34.032 --> 00:04:37.678
The upload dialog shows the selected
file before it enters the list.

97
00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:41.742
Files can be opened or downloaded,
searched, and sorted.

98
00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:45.561
Available actions include moving files
and adding a file to

99
00:04:45.619 --> 00:04:46.293
Documents.

100
00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:50.240
Shared storage does not itself submit
a requirement or create a

101
00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.355
faculty review.

102
00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.325
Use Documents and the associated task
for that record.

103
00:04:55.933 --> 00:04:58.812
Timeline presents the milestone
sequence configured for this

104
00:04:58.882 --> 00:04:59.915
research workflow.

105
00:05:00.414 --> 00:05:04.025
Compare completed scope preparation,
the current proposal work, and

106
00:05:04.095 --> 00:05:05.047
later stages.

107
00:05:05.546 --> 00:05:08.994
Inspect available requirements, target
dates, and progress

108
00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:09.772
information.

109
00:05:10.364 --> 00:05:13.743
The sequence comes from the assigned
workflow rather than a separate

110
00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:14.857
personal checklist.

111
00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:19.269
A later stage may remain unavailable
while prerequisites or approval

112
00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:20.430
remain outstanding.

113
00:05:21.022 --> 00:05:24.238
Returning to a task shows the work
associated with that point in the

114
00:05:24.273 --> 00:05:25.005
sequence.

115
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.711
Defense displays the project's
readiness and defense-related

116
00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:29.350
records.

117
00:05:29.942 --> 00:05:32.845
No defense session has been created
for this prepared Researcher

118
00:05:32.903 --> 00:05:33.611
workspace.

119
00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:37.581
When an authorized session is
available, its schedule, panel,

120
00:05:37.709 --> 00:05:41.378
published manuscript, and released
result can appear in the defense

121
00:05:41.436 --> 00:05:41.889
record.

122
00:05:42.481 --> 00:05:44.884
This example shows the current
readiness state.

123
00:05:45.314 --> 00:05:48.635
It does not create a session or show
panelist controls.

124
00:05:49.233 --> 00:05:52.135
My Grades separates Class Grades from
Defense Grades.

125
00:05:52.565 --> 00:05:55.944
Open each view and inspect its
publication or release state.

126
00:05:56.443 --> 00:05:59.717
This example has no published class
grade or released defense

127
00:05:59.752 --> 00:06:00.274
result.

128
00:06:00.866 --> 00:06:03.943
When results are released, the
permitted components and reviewer

129
00:06:04.001 --> 00:06:06.230
information appear in the
corresponding view.

130
00:06:06.822 --> 00:06:10.781
An unreleased result is unavailable,
rather than a score of zero.

131
00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:15.198
Consultations contains the prepared
proposal revision consultation

132
00:06:15.372 --> 00:06:17.764
and controls for requesting a
consultation.

133
00:06:18.356 --> 00:06:21.886
Inspect its topic, date, time, and
status.

134
00:06:22.478 --> 00:06:25.996
The request form collects a discussion
topic, preferred schedule,

135
00:06:26.054 --> 00:06:26.970
and meeting mode.

136
00:06:27.655 --> 00:06:31.208
A request and a scheduled consultation
represent different states.

137
00:06:31.638 --> 00:06:35.051
The walkthrough opens the form without
creating another booking.

138
00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:38.999
Open the consultation notes or chat
control to inspect its record

139
00:06:39.022 --> 00:06:39.522
area.

140
00:06:40.021 --> 00:06:43.051
This consultation has no transcript or
imported chat.

141
00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.872
The import controls accept supplied
text;

142
00:06:46.244 --> 00:06:48.577
they do not demonstrate automatic
transcription.

143
00:06:49.077 --> 00:06:52.177
When a connected meeting is available,
its meeting information is

144
00:06:52.223 --> 00:06:53.164
displayed here.

145
00:06:53.849 --> 00:06:57.088
Previous consultation records depend
on completed or imported

146
00:06:57.123 --> 00:06:57.958
activity.

147
00:06:58.567 --> 00:07:01.574
Calendar displays events available to
your account for the selected

148
00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:02.201
period.

149
00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:06.102
Inspect the scheduled consultation and
any deadline or academic

150
00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:07.878
event returned for this project.

151
00:07:08.563 --> 00:07:11.698
Open an event to read its details and
related information.

152
00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:14.601
Calendar views provide different date
ranges;

153
00:07:14.972 --> 00:07:17.747
the presence of an event depends on
the underlying record.

154
00:07:18.246 --> 00:07:21.056
Defense events will not appear here
before a defense has been

155
00:07:21.079 --> 00:07:21.880
scheduled.

156
00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.565
Messages provides conversations and
invitations from permitted

157
00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:26.413
participants.

158
00:07:26.912 --> 00:07:30.151
The prepared workspace starts without
a conversation history or

159
00:07:30.232 --> 00:07:31.405
pending invitations.

160
00:07:31.997 --> 00:07:35.248
Researchers can enter conversations
through received invitations;

161
00:07:35.678 --> 00:07:38.627
creating a group conversation is a
faculty control.

162
00:07:39.056 --> 00:07:42.446
An empty conversation list does not
demonstrate a live exchange with

163
00:07:42.481 --> 00:07:43.398
an adviser.

164
00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.553
Inbox uses correspondence threads,
folders, and drafts.

165
00:07:48.145 --> 00:07:51.883
Open its compose area to inspect
recipients, subject, and message

166
00:07:51.918 --> 00:07:54.147
fields, then close it without sending.

167
00:07:54.577 --> 00:07:56.957
This example does not send
correspondence.

168
00:07:57.456 --> 00:08:00.997
Inbox threads and group conversations
are separate communication

169
00:08:01.055 --> 00:08:01.786
areas.

170
00:08:02.367 --> 00:08:06.071
Notifications contains dashboard
updates, account notices, and

171
00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:07.197
earlier notices.

172
00:08:07.696 --> 00:08:09.995
Filters distinguish read and unread
items.

173
00:08:10.424 --> 00:08:13.129
Opening a notice follows its
configured destination;

174
00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:16.020
the prepared notices link to the
dashboard.

175
00:08:16.633 --> 00:08:19.594
Profile shows the account information
associated with the

176
00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.325
Researcher.

177
00:08:20.917 --> 00:08:24.563
Settings includes account information,
appearance, and notification

178
00:08:24.621 --> 00:08:25.364
preferences.

179
00:08:25.956 --> 00:08:28.742
Notification preferences here are
stored in the browser.

180
00:08:29.334 --> 00:08:32.493
Open Appearance to inspect the
available color themes and display

181
00:08:32.551 --> 00:08:33.003
modes.

182
00:08:33.503 --> 00:08:36.637
Available account changes depend on
the current account and access

183
00:08:36.695 --> 00:08:37.531
rules.

184
00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:40.768
That concludes the ADVISIO Researcher
walkthrough.

185
00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:44.495
Return to any section whenever you
need a refresher while using the

186
00:08:44.518 --> 00:08:45.378
platform.
